thumbstick to switch between smooth movement and stepped movement (for those who might find smooth movement unsettling)\n - Click the right thumbstick to switch between smooth rotation and snap turns.\n - A new laser aim pointer to aid lining up shots\n - When the shot is lined up, you can now choose to hold the Y button on the left controller to enable Autoplay. Release the Y button to play the shot with the desired power (for those who are unable to use the standard cueing action effectively)\n - Now defaults to use the Novice Cue with minimal spin, to give beginners better shot accuracy.", "created_date": 1648679461, "id": "7383773305026405", "version": "1.09", "version_code": 5, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "7050023918401347", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "7422605814476487"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "684780659564038"}]}, "change_log": "The latest update adds:\n - Click the left thumbstick to switch between smooth movement and stepped movement (for those who might find smooth movement unsettling)\n - Click the right thumbstick to switch between smooth rotation and snap turns.\n - A new laser aim pointer to aid lining up shots\n - When the shot is lined up and the laser pointer showing, you can now choose to hold the Y button on the left controller to enable Autoplay. Release the Y button to play the shot with the desired power (for those who are unable to use the standard cueing action effectively)\n - Now defaults to use the Novice Cue with minimal spin, to give beginners better shot accuracy.", "created_date": 1648602519, "i